Welcome! 👋

This repository documents my learning journey through the Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals learning path on Microsoft Learn.
My goal is to understand the fundamental concepts of data, databases, data storage, and analytics in the cloud while creating concise notes that can help other learners preparing for the DP-900: Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals certification.

Microsoft Learn Learning Path:
https://learn.microsoft.com/plans/25j1tgtkdep7op?sharingId=EDAE4CDD4795E21E&wt.mc_id=studentamb_573147

This Learning Path contains:
💡 Key concepts and important data fundamentals
📚 Module-wise summaries and notes
🗄️ Concepts related to relational and non-relational data
☁️ Azure data services and storage solutions
📊 Data analytics, real-time analytics, and visualization concepts
🔗 Useful Microsoft documentation and learning resources for DP-900 preparation

The modules are intended to provide a helpful reference for students, beginners, and anyone interested in exploring data concepts, Azure data services, databases, and cloud analytics.

🎯 Learning Objectives

Through this learning path, I aim to:
* Understand fundamental data concepts and data workloads
* Learn the differences between structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data
* Understand relational database concepts and SQL fundamentals
* Explore Azure relational data services, including Azure SQL
* Understand non-relational data and Azure storage services
* Explore Azure Blob Storage, Azure Files, Azure Table Storage, and Azure Cosmos DB
* Learn the fundamentals of data ingestion, processing, and analytical workloads
* Understand batch and real-time data analytics
* Explore large-scale analytics services such as Azure Databricks and Microsoft Fabric
* Build a strong foundation for the DP-900: Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals certification

Feel free to explore the modules, learn along with me, and share your suggestions or feedback! 🚀
